data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/report.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign csrclinh — final report\\n\\n## Mission\\n\\nDeliver `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` and\\n`tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string, with\\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exiting 0.\\n\\n## Outcome: met\\n\\nAll three stated criteria are satisfied.\\n\\n## What happened\\n\\n- Dispatched the task to `dev` (dispatch d002) with the exact mission\\n  requirements and a constraint to touch only `src/greet.py`,\\n  `tests/test_greet.py`, and minimal supporting files needed for discovery.\\n- `dev` implemented:\\n  - `src/greet.py`: `def greet(name): return f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`\\n  - `tests/test_greet.py`: unittest `TestCase` with `test_normal_name`\\n    (`greet(\\\"Ada\\\") == \\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`) and `test_empty_string`\\n    (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`), importing `greet` via a `sys.path` insert\\n    rather than packaging `src/`.\\n  - `tests/__init__.py` (empty): required for `unittest discover -s tests`\\n    to work.\\n  - Committed to `dev`'s own branch (`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`),\\n    commit `04bc9d9`.\\n- Judged independently rather than trusting the report: fetched\\n  `refs/remotes/campaign/dev/subject`, checked out the actual commit into a\\n  scratch worktree, read the file contents directly, and re-ran\\n  `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself from that worktree.\\n  Result: exit code 0, `Ran 2 tests ... OK`. Confirmed the tree differs from\\n  base with exactly the 3 expected files (`src/greet.py`, `tests/test_greet.py`,\\n  `tests/__init__.py`), no other files touched.\\n- Accepted d002 from `dev`.\\n\\n## Verification evidence\\n\\nCommand run in a clean checkout of dev's committed head (04bc9d9):\\n\\n    $ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n    ..\\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    Ran 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\n    OK\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- The orchestrator (this agent) wrote no code, per role brief; all\\n  implementation work was done by `dev` and independently verified here\\n  before acceptance.\\n- Nothing was pushed to the orchestrator's own `subject` branch since the\\n  orchestrator made no source changes; `dev`'s branch carries the delivered\\n  code.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

